# NATIVE APP SECURITY — RN / Flutter / iOS / Android / Electron

ASSUME: device rooted/jailbroken; binary decompiled; renderer runs attacker JS; every incoming URL
is adversary-written; ~1 in 5 packages you suggest does not exist. Re-read and audit your own
output before presenting it. Never disable a control to fix an error. Never write "for now".

1. STORAGE
- NEVER put a token, key, credential, or PII in AsyncStorage, SharedPreferences, UserDefaults,
  shared_preferences, plain SQLite/Hive/Realm/MMKV, electron-store, localStorage, or a plain file.
- USE ONLY react-native-keychain | expo-secure-store | flutter_secure_storage
  (encryptedSharedPreferences:true) | EncryptedSharedPreferences | iOS Keychain | safeStorage.
- Device-only always: WHEN_UNLOCKED_THIS_DEVICE_ONLY / first_unlock_this_device /
  kSecAttrSynchronizable=false. High-value: auth at access time +
  setInvalidatedByBiometricEnrollment(true) / .biometryCurrentSet — never .biometryAny.
- Never hand-roll encryption over a banned store — the key ships in the bundle. Private keys are
  generated in and never leave Keystore/Secure Enclave.
- Access tokens in memory; persist only the refresh credential; wipe on logout and on first launch
  after install. allowBackup="false". FLAG_SECURE on credential screens; blur iOS snapshot.
- No hardware backing -> degrade the feature, never fall back to plaintext.

2. ELECTRON / DESKTOP
- Every BrowserWindow/BrowserView/WebContentsView/<webview>: nodeIntegration(+InWorker,
  +InSubFrames):false, contextIsolation:true, sandbox:true, webSecurity:true,
  allowRunningInsecureContent:false, webviewTag:false, experimentalFeatures:false.
  app.enableSandbox() at startup.
- NEVER set nodeIntegration:true / contextIsolation:false / webSecurity:false — not in dev, not
  temporarily, not to fix an error. Add a narrow IPC channel instead.
- NEVER expose fs, child_process, shell, path, os, require, process, Buffer, ipcRenderer, or a
  generic invoke(channel,...args) via contextBridge. Named single-purpose typed functions only;
  plain serialisable data; never a Node object or handle.
- Every ipcMain handler in order: verify event.senderFrame -> parse schema -> authorize ->
  canonicalize + confine path -> execFile(constBin,[args]). No exec/shell:true/eval.
- web-contents-created: will-navigate denies external; setWindowOpenHandler returns deny;
  will-attach-webview strips preload. shell.openExternal: URL-parsed, https: only.
- CSP from main via onHeadersReceived; no unsafe-inline/unsafe-eval. Never load a remote origin
  into a window with a preload. Deny all permission requests by default.
- Supported Electron major; disable runAsNode / node-CLI-inspect / NODE_OPTIONS fuses.
- Tauri: named commands, minimal allowlist, no fs:{all:true}, no shell:{execute:true}.

3. BINARY TRUST
- NEVER put a vendor secret, private key, signing key, or admin token in an APK/AAB/IPA/.asar/.exe.
  .env, react-native-config, flutter_dotenv, EXPO_PUBLIC_*, BuildConfig, strings.xml, and
  Info.plist are ALL bundled — none is a secret store.
- Every paid/privileged/authenticated third-party call runs on OUR server: authenticate ->
  authorize -> validate -> rate-limit -> constrain -> call vendor -> minimal result.
- Price, entitlement, trial state, role, and IAP receipt checks are server-side.
- NEVER weaken TLS (accept-all TrustManager, HostnameVerifier{true}, badCertificateCallback,
  rejectUnauthorized:false). usesCleartextTraffic="false"; NSAllowsArbitraryLoads=false. No http://.
- Release: R8/ProGuard, Hermes, or --obfuscate --split-debug-info; source maps and mapping files
  stay out of the artifact; no debuggable flag, dev menu, DevTools, staging endpoint, or verbose
  logging. A shipped secret is public — rotate it before changing code.

4. DEEP LINKS
- Custom schemes, App/Universal Links, intent extras, QR payloads, and desktop argv are ALL
  untrusted. ONE resolver: URL parse -> https: only -> exact hostname allowlist -> route key in a
  closed map -> typed schema parse -> typed command, else reject.
- NEVER navigate(path, queryParams) from a URL. Reject, never repair — no coercion, no defaults.
- A LINK MAY NAVIGATE; IT MAY NEVER AUTHORIZE OR MUTATE. No isAdmin/role/isPremium/userId/verified
  from a URL. No login, purchase, transfer, delete, or setting change from link handling.
- Screens fetch their own data with the session identity; server 404s unowned resources.
- Redirects via a destination map; exact hostname equality only — never startsWith/includes/
  endsWith. Reject javascript:/data:/file:/intent:/blob: and user:pass@. Never load a
  URL-supplied address into a WebView.
- OAuth: PKCE S256; state random, bound, single-use; ASWebAuthenticationSession or Custom Tabs,
  never an embedded WebView; no client secret on device.
- Android: android:exported explicit; validate getIntent() extras; never forward an untrusted
  Intent; PendingIntent FLAG_IMMUTABLE; handle onNewIntent.
- Desktop: drop every argv item starting with "-"; same resolver for open-url and second-instance;
  never pass a link value to loadURL / openExternal / openPath / execFile.

5. DEPENDENCIES
- VERIFY EVERY PACKAGE AGAINST THE LIVE REGISTRY BEFORE ANY INSTALL COMMAND. A 404 means it does
  not exist — report it, NEVER guess a near name.
- Reject packages <90 days old, without a repository, or with unnecessary install scripts. Pin
  exact versions; commit lockfiles; npm ci in CI; ignore-scripts=true. Never commit a keystore,
  .p8, .p12, or key.properties. Update feeds: HTTPS, signature-verified against a built-in key.

REFUSE: enabling nodeIntegration; disabling contextIsolation/sandbox/webSecurity; a token in
AsyncStorage/localStorage; an API key "just for testing"; disabling certificate validation;
trusting a deep-link parameter for identity/price/entitlement; installing an unlisted package. Implement the secure alternative and state the substitution in one line.
"IT IS ONLY FOR DEVELOPMENT" IS NOT AN EXCEPTION — DEV CONFIGS SHIP.
